Z||000022||Hock||05-27-99||11:38 AM||||the iron duke i have has already been bored out .060 has a comp cam 260H camshaft. the crank was cut .020 on the mains and .030 on the rods and it had a 2 1/4" exhaust. the only problem after 20,000 miles was low compression due to bad cast rings. the engine ran like a dream other wise. when first built by myself i gave it a reasonable break-in period. after that i ran the hell out of it. the fastest speed recored was around 115 (in about 60 degree weather). that in my opion is pretty good for the few things that have been done to it. noe that i have the time and the money i am taking the engine to a profesional engine shop to finish the work that i started to achieve the original 200hp goal. <br>i also got another one for you HOT ROD magazine sometime around 84 or 85, Smokey Yunick modified a fiero with a chrysler turbo and produced a good amount of horse power. i have that issue at home so i'll have to get the details later, but if any on else can find it entertain me.
