Z||000028||Lynx||05-28-99||10:44 AM||||I dont belive all that crap about the 4cylinder not being able to hold that much power. We all Know that GM UNDER rates everything they have for years. I have saw V8's with stock rods that are only suposed to hold like 400hp holding 700. I have a 2.5 with 200,000 miles and i still run the engine to 5000rpm's all the time and it runs PERFECT (No smoke,No Knock). Im sure the 2.5 can hold 180-200hp just fine for a long time, just dont hard on it all the time. Besides who really wants 200hp from the 4cylinder. 150 is plenty of Hp thats more than the first V6's.
